speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise in the House today on behalf of all residents of the City of Port Coquitlam in British Columbia, both past and present. It was 75 years ago that Port Coquitlam was officially incorporated as a City.
In honour of this occasion, I would like to read into the record books an excerpt from the Mayor's Proclamation:
And whereas on March 7th, 1913 the said Letters Patent under the Great Seal were so issued thereby creating the "Corporation of the City of Port Coquitlam".
And whereas exactly seventy-five years have elapsed between the date of the Letters Patent and March 7th, 1988;
Now therefore be it resolved that by virtue of the powers vested in me as Mayor of the Corporation of the City of Port Coquitlam, I Leonard M. Traboulay, do now declare March 7th, 1988 to be "Diamond Anniversary Day" in the City of Port Coquitlam and do urge all our citizens to take part in the many festivities planned for the balance of our Diamond Jubilee Year;
I am honoured, as the city's Member of Parliament, to invite everyone from Port Coquitlam and the surrounding communities, and people from all over Canada to join in the festivities and celebrate the Diamond Anniversary of the City of Port Coquitlam.
